  // Paldea as plan 34 · PD1 opens it, hand-built at about a third of the original's distances (plan 34 · decision 1)
  // from public descriptions of Scarlet and Violet and memory of play, nothing traced or taken: Cabo Poco on its cape in
  // the far south-west, the player's house and the president's on the hill over the sea; Poco Path north along the
  // cliffs past the lighthouse, with the beach under them and Inlet Grotto in their foot; Los Platos, the crossroads
  // village; the South Province's first area of fields; and Mesagoza at the head of its rise, the academy on its hill at
  // the top of the stairs. x runs east, z south, y up, in metres; a chunk is 32 m. The rest of the region grows north and
  // east of these chunks in later sessions (plan 34 · PD3 on), so nothing here has to move
  "region": "Paldea",
  "chunks": [-26, -27, 20, 1],
  // Only the land the areas hold is baked (plan 34 · PD3, the user's option b of 2026-11-14): every chunk an area
  // touches and the ring of chunks round it, so the hills between the places and the sea beyond them are never baked
  "bakeRing": 1,
  "baseHeight": 1.2,
  // Ridden (plan 34 · PD2): its navigation mesh holds the mount's hops, high jumps, climbs and glides
  "mount": true,
